{
    "background_story": "Muffinhead was a regal feline with a penchant for the finer things in life. Born in the late nineteenth century, she was the beloved companion of a wealthy socialite in Victorian-era London. Muffinhead spent her days lounging on plush cushions, chasing the occasional mouse, and purring contentedly as her owner stroked her soft fur. As the Industrial Revolution transformed the city, Muffinhead remained a steadfast symbol of elegance and refinement. She would often sit by the window, watching the horse-drawn carriages roll by, and the gas lamps flicker to life. Despite the changing times, Muffinhead's owner made sure she remained a cherished fixture of their household, indulging her every whim and spoiling her rotten. And so, Muffinhead lived out her days in luxury, a true lady of the nineteenth century.",
